{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"eaae8ca9c8c87c84bda13e91e48816ea56f367cbd3b762b15e2c54b220885a37","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira adapter (AcliClient search cache)","key_entities":["AcliClient.search_issues","AcliClient._search_cache","AcliClient.invalidate_search_cache","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py","tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_search_cache_freshness.py","bind_operation_runtime","_backend_registry.select_backend"],"problem_keywords":["cache freshness","memoization","unbounded cache","negative caching","stale results","Jira search"],"propositions":["AcliClient.search_issues memoizes all results per JQL indefinitely with no TTL or invalidation, including negative (empty) answers, causing callers to receive permanently stale results on re-query.","Multiple sites in the codebase work around the missing freshness mechanism by directly mutating the private _search_cache attribute, violating encapsulation and remaining undocumented.","An AcliClient instance and its cache live for exactly one reconcile pass in production, as each pass constructs a fresh client via bind_operation_runtime and select_backend with no caching.","Negative-to-positive flips in Jira query results become invisible when cached indefinitely, as demonstrated by bug d30c where an index-visibility poll's second JQL attempt never reached Jira."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787875357326037001,"uuid":"94022c3c-b2d4-40df-8051-06c63c4883e1"}